<div class="bg-white px-6 py-16 sm:px-8 lg:px-8">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
    <.link navigate={~p"/"}>
      <img class="h-10" src={~p"/images/full-logo.svg"} alt="Spendable" />
    </.link>

    <h1 class="mt-10 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-700">
      <p>
        Spendable is a budgeting app. Your financial data is yours - it is never sold, rented,
        or shared with advertisers, and it is not used to build a profile of you.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900">What we store</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">When you sign in with Google we store your Google account identifier
          and your profile image so we can recognise you on your next visit.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          When you connect a bank through Plaid we store the access token for that connection
          along with the institution, your account names, masked account numbers, balances and
          types, and the transactions on those accounts - their description, amount, date and
          whether they are still pending.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Everything else - your budgets, allocations and splits - is created by you inside
          the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900">Who we share it with</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Nobody, other than the services required to run the app: Google for sign-in, Plaid for
          bank connections, and our own hosting and error-monitoring infrastructure. We do not
          sell your data and we do not share it for advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900">Deleting your data</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You can disconnect a bank at any time from the Banks page, which removes the stored
          access token for that connection. To delete your account and everything in it, email <a
            class="font-semibold text-brand"
            href="mailto:support@spendable.money"
          >support@spendable.money</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900">Source code</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Spendable is open source. You can read exactly what it does at <a
            class="font-semibold text-brand"
            href="https://github.com/michaelst/spendable"
            target="_blank"
          >
            github.com/michaelst/spendable
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
